 worked_example="""Assess two simulated fly studies with a **custom adapted SYRCLE** protocol: (1) 'Random housing' interpreted as 'were vials randomly positioned in the incubator?'; (2) 'Blinding of investigators' interpreted as 'was the person scoring deaths unaware of group?'. Study A: methods state randomised positions and blinded scoring -> low/low with quotes. Study B: no information -> unclear/unclear. Record the interpretation rules in the protocol, then rate. Reviewer 2 rates B 'high' for blinding because the experimenter scored deaths; disagreement is resolved by discussion: judgement 'high' because the report states the experimenter handled both groups and scored (quote p. 4). Resolution is logged.""",
